-- The relational middle-end's reference seed.
--
-- This module is BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC.md Appendix A verbatim, and the Catala
-- study's Appendix A before that, so the three bridges can be compared on one
-- source. The Debug golden beside it (expected/benefit) should be recognisably
-- the same program as the Prolog in that appendix: two clauses for
-- `eligible for benefit` (the OR split, with the UNLESS as a complemented
-- comparison copied into both), the WHERE helper as its own predicate under its
-- own name, and the value-position IF as a guarded clause pair whose second arm
-- carries a materialised negation.
--
-- ONE DEVIATION FROM THE APPENDIX, and it is not cosmetic: both `@export`
-- annotations were moved ABOVE their `GIVEN`. The appendix writes them between
-- GIVETH and the definition head, and measured on this tree that placement does
-- not reliably attach: with the appendix's exact text
-- `L4.Export.getExportedFunctions` returns ONE of the two decisions, not both,
-- so half the appendix's Prolog would be unreachable from any entry point and a
-- golden taken from it would silently pin half a program. Every `@export` in the
-- in-tree corpus (jl4/examples/openfisca/*.l4) sits above `GIVEN`, which is what
-- this file does. Reported as a conflict against BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC Appendix A.
--
-- Each directive below carries its L4-oracle value on the line after it, as a
-- `-- L4 oracle ==>` comment produced by `l4 run benefit.l4`. That is the
-- differential harness's expectation and it lives HERE rather than in the
-- emitted program, because BLAWX-EXPORT-SPEC R11 keeps the oracle outside the
-- artifact: a bridge bug that moved actual and expected together would
-- otherwise pass silently. One place, not two — a second copy in this header
-- would be a claim nobody re-checks.

DECLARE Applicant HAS
    age       IS A NUMBER
    income    IS A NUMBER
    isVeteran IS A BOOLEAN

@export
GIVEN a IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible for benefit` IF
       a's age AT LEAST 65
    OR a's isVeteran
    UNLESS a's income GREATER THAN 100000

@export
GIVEN a IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A NUMBER
`benefit amount` a MEANS
    IF `eligible for benefit` a THEN 1000 PLUS bonus ELSE 0
    WHERE bonus MEANS IF a's isVeteran THEN 250 ELSE 0

#EVAL `benefit amount` (Applicant WITH age IS 70, income IS 50000, isVeteran IS FALSE)
-- L4 oracle ==> 1000

-- The two #ASSERT directives below are the committed witnesses for the R11
-- ruling's other half: an #ASSERT emits BOTH a test (like #EVAL) and a
-- `false :- not goal(...).` constraint inside that test, runtime-checked on
-- the Blawx side. One exercises the boolean shape, one the EQUALS shape.
#ASSERT `eligible for benefit` (Applicant WITH age IS 70, income IS 50000, isVeteran IS FALSE)
-- L4 oracle ==> assertion satisfied

#ASSERT `benefit amount` (Applicant WITH age IS 30, income IS 50000, isVeteran IS TRUE) EQUALS 1250
-- L4 oracle ==> assertion satisfied
